context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:1:# Workflow
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:2:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:3:## Controller sequence
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:4:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:5:The issue-1 implementation is a single-run, non-resumable controller. It first
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:6:parses every required level-two brief section and verifies that the target does
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:7:not exist. It builds the initial workspace in a temporary sibling directory
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:8:and commits that directory with an operating-system no-replace rename only
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:9:after initialization succeeds. A concurrently created directory or symlink is
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:10:never replaced.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:11:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:12:```mermaid
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:13:flowchart TD
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:14:    v[Validate brief and new target] --> i[Atomically initialize run]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:15:    i --> pm[Start persistent PM in tmux]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:16:    pm --> r[Researcher]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:17:    r --> s[Story Editor]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:18:    s --> w[Writer creates candidate 001]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:19:    w --> e[Fresh Evidence Reviewer]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:20:    e --> pe[PM classifies findings]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:21:    pe -->|no must-fix| sr[Fresh Story Reviewer]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:22:    sr --> ps[PM classifies findings]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:23:    ps -->|no must-fix| c[Fresh Clarity Reviewer]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:24:    c --> pc[PM classifies findings]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:25:    pc -->|no must-fix| cp[Fresh Copy Reviewer]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:26:    cp --> pp[PM classifies findings]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:27:    pp -->|all gates pass| f[Exact-copy candidate to article.md]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:28:    pe -->|validated must-fix| b{Candidate below 003?}
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:29:    ps -->|validated must-fix| b
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:30:    pc -->|validated must-fix| b
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:31:    pp -->|validated must-fix| b
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:32:    b -->|yes| rw[Writer creates next candidate]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:33:    rw --> e
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:34:    b -->|no| blocked[Block and preserve artifacts]
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:35:    pe -->|human judgment| blocked
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:36:    ps -->|human judgment| blocked
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:37:    pc -->|human judgment| blocked
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:38:    pp -->|human judgment| blocked
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:39:```
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:40:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:41:Review lenses are never parallel. A must-fix stops the remaining lenses for
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:42:that candidate and the replacement restarts at Evidence. Optional and invalid
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:43:findings do not consume a candidate. A human-judgment decision blocks.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:44:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:45:## Artifact gates
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:46:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:47:Go does not treat an agent's final message or process exit as completion. A
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:48:worker must exit successfully before Go reads its owned files, and may advance
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:49:only when those files exist and pass validation:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:50:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:51:- research has non-empty sources and a claim ledger naming Fact, Firsthand
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:52:  observation, Inference, Opinion, and Unresolved;
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:53:- the outline records Purpose, Supporting evidence, and Reader takeaway;
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:54:- each candidate is non-empty and has no TODO placeholder;
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:55:- reviewer JSON has an allowed status, exact lens and SHA-256 revision, unique
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:56:  complete findings, plus a report with the same finding fields;
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:57:- PM decisions cover every finding, use allowed classifications, match the
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:58:  current revision, explain every invalid classification, and preserve the
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:59:  exact accepted classifications and routing outcome of every earlier lens.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:60:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:61:A reviewer changing its candidate is an artifact-contract failure. Stale lens
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:62:or revision metadata is rejected rather than retried into a passing state.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:63:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:64:## Lifecycle and terminal states
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:65:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:66:The PM starts before research, atomically publishes its protocol-ready marker,
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:67:and remains active while Go starts one worker window at a time. Go verifies
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:68:both the PM Codex process identity and this application-level handshake before
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:69:starting any worker, and rechecks PM liveness before accepting worker output.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:70:Each role runs in a fresh private workspace outside the run
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:71:directory. Go stages only its allowed inputs, waits for a natural successful
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:72:exit marker and tmux-window disappearance, validates output without following
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:73:symlinks, and then copies regular files into the run. The marker is published
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:74:by a same-directory temporary-file rename only after the Codex process and its
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:75:descendants are gone. The controller-private runner, ancestry ownership
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:76:manifests/ready records,
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:77:live PM requests, and other launch-critical state are siblings of—not children
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:78:of—agent workspaces. A default-deny macOS native sandbox gives agents only
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:79:system runtime reads plus their current workspace and isolated Codex home; it
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:80:denies unrelated host, durable-run, prior-lens, PM, and controller-private
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:81:access. Controller-only test paths never become sandbox rules or agent
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:82:environment variables. The private runner follows parent/child edges through
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:83:the native process table and durably records precise kernel process identities
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:84:for the invocation ancestry, including children that create a new session or
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:85:process group, clear their environment, or execute a protected system binary.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:86:Cleanup opens stable kernel process handles before signaling each recorded
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:87:identity, so a reused bare PID is never treated as owned. Each lens uses a
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:88:fresh Codex invocation.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:89:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:90:Every agent has the configured timeout, and tmux lifecycle commands have their
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:91:own short bound. The controller enforces both a context timer and an absolute
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:92:wall-clock deadline, so host sleep or a missing runner completion marker cannot
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:93:extend an invocation past its contract. A timeout, premature exit, malformed
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:94:artifact, stale review,
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:95:cleanup failure, human decision, or exhausted candidate budget sets an
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:96:actionable `workflow.json.block_reason`. Success requires verified absence of
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:97:the dedicated tmux session and every invocation identity. On success the
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:98:controller also requires the persistent PM to still be live,
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:99:then revalidates the candidate hash, every final review, each PM request
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:100:binding, and each accepted classification list before publishing `article.md`
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:101:and durably persisting the succeeded state. A failure during that terminal
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:102:transition removes `article.md`, records blocked state, attempts private-state
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:103:cleanup even if blocked-state persistence fails. Ordinarily the blocked path
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:104:also verifies that no PM, worker, or detached descendant remains. If signaling
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:105:or absence verification itself fails, the controller records that cleanup
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:106:failure, deletes every staged Codex credential, archives the available audit
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:107:files, and preserves only non-secret ownership/control state so cleanup can be
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:108:diagnosed and retried. That exceptional blocked result does not claim process
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:109:absence.
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:110:
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:111:Parallel runs, resume after controller restart, and editing completed runs are
context/source-hints/002-workflow.md:112:not implemented.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:1:# write-uuter
context/source-hints/001-README.md:2:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:3:`write-uuter` is a Go CLI that turns a Markdown brief into a reviewed article
context/source-hints/001-README.md:4:while preserving the evidence, outline, candidates, reviews, and PM decisions
context/source-hints/001-README.md:5:that produced it.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:6:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:7:## Requirements
context/source-hints/001-README.md:8:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:9:- Go 1.26 or later to build
context/source-hints/001-README.md:10:- cgo enabled plus the Xcode Command Line Tools to build for macOS; Darwin
context/source-hints/001-README.md:11:  no-cgo builds are rejected because audit-token signaling is mandatory
context/source-hints/001-README.md:12:- tmux on the host
context/source-hints/001-README.md:13:- an installed and authenticated Codex CLI for real runs
context/source-hints/001-README.md:14:- macOS for real runs; the controller uses the native Seatbelt sandbox to
context/source-hints/001-README.md:15:  enforce role filesystem isolation
context/source-hints/001-README.md:16:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:17:No third-party Go packages are used.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:18:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:19:Linux cross-builds are supported, but Linux execution fails closed until an
context/source-hints/001-README.md:20:equivalent native read-isolation backend is implemented.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:21:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:22:## Build and test
context/source-hints/001-README.md:23:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:24:```sh
context/source-hints/001-README.md:25:make build
context/source-hints/001-README.md:26:make verify
context/source-hints/001-README.md:27:```
context/source-hints/001-README.md:28:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:29:The tests build the CLI and execute it as a subprocess against a deterministic
context/source-hints/001-README.md:30:fake Codex executable inside real tmux sessions. They do not require network
context/source-hints/001-README.md:31:access or Codex authentication.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:32:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:33:## Run
context/source-hints/001-README.md:34:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:35:From the repository root:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:36:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:37:```sh
context/source-hints/001-README.md:38:./bin/write-uuter run \
context/source-hints/001-README.md:39:  --brief examples/brief.md \
context/source-hints/001-README.md:40:  --run-dir smoke-runs/my-run
context/source-hints/001-README.md:41:```
context/source-hints/001-README.md:42:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:43:The run directory must not already exist. Its parent is created when needed.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:44:On success the command exits 0 and `smoke-runs/my-run/article.md` is a non-empty
context/source-hints/001-README.md:45:exact copy of the candidate accepted by all four reviewers. A runtime failure,
context/source-hints/001-README.md:46:timeout, exhausted third candidate, or need for human judgment exits non-zero
context/source-hints/001-README.md:47:and preserves a `workflow.json` whose status is `blocked`. Invalid briefs and
context/source-hints/001-README.md:48:existing targets exit non-zero without creating or changing a run.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:49:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:50:Operational options:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:51:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:52:```text
context/source-hints/001-README.md:53:--codex <path>       Codex executable (default: codex)
context/source-hints/001-README.md:54:--tmux <path>        tmux executable (default: tmux)
context/source-hints/001-README.md:55:--timeout <duration> Per-agent artifact timeout (default: 10m)
context/source-hints/001-README.md:56:--prompts-dir <path> Checked-in prompt directory; an explicit value is binding
context/source-hints/001-README.md:57:```
context/source-hints/001-README.md:58:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:59:The brief requires these case-insensitive level-two headings; all except
context/source-hints/001-README.md:60:`Source hints` need non-whitespace content:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:61:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:62:```text
context/source-hints/001-README.md:63:Question, Audience, Provisional takeaway, Scope, Out of scope,
context/source-hints/001-README.md:64:Publication target, Constraints, Done when, Source hints
context/source-hints/001-README.md:65:```
context/source-hints/001-README.md:66:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:67:Relative source-hint paths are resolved from the directory containing the
context/source-hints/001-README.md:68:input brief. The process working directory is the content root. If present,
context/source-hints/001-README.md:69:`STYLE.md`, `style-guide.md`, or `docs/style-guide.md` under that root is staged
context/source-hints/001-README.md:70:only for the Copy reviewer; prompt bundles may live elsewhere.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:71:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:72:## Runtime model
context/source-hints/001-README.md:73:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:74:Go owns state transitions, validation, revision hashes, timeouts, and process
context/source-hints/001-README.md:75:cleanup. One long-lived PM Codex process and at most one worker run in a
context/source-hints/001-README.md:76:dedicated tmux session. Each process receives a separate controller-created
context/source-hints/001-README.md:77:workspace outside the durable run directory; Go copies in only the role's
context/source-hints/001-README.md:78:contracted context and copies validated regular-file outputs back. A native
context/source-hints/001-README.md:79:sandbox denies agents access to the durable run, other role workspaces, and
context/source-hints/001-README.md:80:controller-private launch state. Codex's inner sandbox is disabled because
context/source-hints/001-README.md:81:macOS does not support nesting it inside the stricter controller sandbox. Go
context/source-hints/001-README.md:82:owns each invocation with native stable process identities (pidfds on Linux and
context/source-hints/001-README.md:83:audit tokens on macOS). The macOS sandbox permits forks only from the staged
context/source-hints/001-README.md:84:single-use Codex client. Only the original host `sandbox-exec` transition may
context/source-hints/001-README.md:85:enter that client; sandboxed descendants cannot execute either the privileged
context/source-hints/001-README.md:86:client or `sandbox-exec` again. Model-invoked runtimes therefore cannot reacquire
context/source-hints/001-README.md:87:client authority or double-fork out of controller ownership; a
context/source-hints/001-README.md:88:controller-private manifest tracks the remaining descendants.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:89:The controller requires a live PM/worker handshake and publishes completion
context/source-hints/001-README.md:90:through an atomic marker only after descendants are gone.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:91:Researcher, Story Editor, Writer, then fresh Evidence, Story, Clarity, and Copy
context/source-hints/001-README.md:92:reviewer processes run sequentially. Reviewers never receive the run directory
context/source-hints/001-README.md:93:or edit candidates. Only PM-validated must-fix findings create a new candidate;
context/source-hints/001-README.md:94:candidate 003 is the hard limit.
context/source-hints/001-README.md:95:
context/source-hints/001-README.md:96:See [workflow](docs/workflow.md), [roles](docs/roles.md), and
context/source-hints/001-README.md:97:[artifacts](docs/artifacts.md) for the exact shipped contracts.

