The sources agree on the core mechanics: Go owns transitions and validation; roles work in isolated staged contexts; four reviewer lenses run sequentially with PM routing between them; and success or blockage is represented by durable artifacts. I’m now turning those points into traceable claims, including explicit limits and unresolved items.
